  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{(2)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
